From 4a65ac9e9d936542331d9198e22316f5820f51b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:10:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 33/42] Liveness texts in five more languages
 (machine-translated), right to left

The 44 liveness keys in app_ar, app_fr, app_hi, app_kn and app_ta.arb,
with the English placeholders. Each file is marked
"@@x-liveness-translation": "machine-translated; needs native-speaker
review" (gen-l10n ignores @@ attributes). The translations reuse each
file's existing terms where they are correct (face, operator,
supervisor, administrator, retry, left/right, exception); the failure
texts stay generic.

Right to left (Arabic):
- The state icons are drawn in a left-to-right Directionality, so the
  turn arrows keep pointing to the user's physical left and right
  (Icons.arrow_back and arrow_forward mirror themselves otherwise).
- The hint, progress and debug-chip paddings are directional.

Debug page: a "UI:" language menu (GlobalProvider.toggleLocale). Without
a backend the login page offers English only.

Tests:
- liveness_l10n_test: all 44 keys in the six ARBs with the English
  placeholders, the note, and every spec key resolving in every locale.
- liveness_page_locale_test: Arabic (right to left, arrows not
  mirrored, banner, progress, tips and buttons placed right to left),
  Hindi, and every state in all six languages without a layout error.
  The arrow test failed before the fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
